---

Parts of parch come from other MIT-licensed work, under the same terms:

- The theme (src/theme.h, src/theme.cpp), the theme lookup
  (src/themefolder.h), the line icons (src/Icon.qml, src/icons.js), the file
  picker (src/filepicker.h, src/portalfilepicker.h, src/portalfilepicker.cpp)
  and the package recipe and install script (pkgbuild/PKGBUILD, bin/install)
  are adapted from sprawl. Copyright (c) 2026 willykev.
- The desktop file picker follows Omacut's, through sprawl; watching the theme
  follows Omacut, reading the whole palette follows Hype, and the control
  states and roles follow the Omarchy shell. Copyright (c) David Heinemeier
  Hansson.
- Additional icon attribution, for line icons that sprawl's set shares with
  Feather: Copyright (c) Cole Bemis.

---

The package also ships two programs parch runs to draw math and diagrams.
They are not part of parch and keep their own licences, installed with them
in /usr/share/licenses/parch/ (licenses/ratex/ in this repository):

- RaTeX (render-svg), which draws TeX math: Copyright (c) erweixin, under
  the MIT License. It carries the KaTeX fonts, Copyright (c) 2009-2010
  Design Science, Inc. and Copyright (c) 2014-2018 Khan Academy, under the
  SIL Open Font License 1.1.
- Merman (merman-cli), which draws Mermaid diagrams: Copyright (c) 2026
  merman contributors, under the MIT License or the Apache License 2.0. It carries work from
  Mermaid, Eclipse ELK (Eclipse Public License 2.0), RaTeX, the KaTeX fonts,
  and the other projects its third-party notices list with their licences.
